            <ArticleTitle>A woman with a painful eruption following liver transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>319-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/tid.12079</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 29-year-old woman with hepatitis C presented 2 years after an orthotopic liver transplant with several weeks of fevers, abdominal pain, nausea, and a painful ulcerated nodular eruption on her abdomen and lower extremities. The patient was evaluated, and her case is presented and the differential discussed.</AbstractText>
